# Frontend environment variables (Vite)
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and edit if you need to override the default behaviour.
# `.env.local` is git-ignored (see `*.local` in .gitignore).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_API_URL - OPTIONAL override for the API base URL.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# You normally do NOT need to set this at all:
#
#   * Local dev  -> `npm run dev` serves the app from Vite, and the
#                   `server.proxy` block in `vite.config.ts` forwards
#                   `/api/*` to http://localhost:8000/* (the `/api` prefix
#                   is stripped, because the FastAPI routes are `/chat`,
#                   `/projects`, `/skills`, `/health`, `/resume/download`
#                   with NO `/api` prefix).
#
#   * Production -> Vercel rewrites `/api/:path*` to the Railway backend
#                   (see `vercel.json`), again stripping the `/api` prefix.
#                   Same-origin, so no CORS and no build-time env var.
#
# Set it only when you want to bypass the proxy and talk to a backend
# directly - e.g. hitting a local backend from a preview build, or pointing
# a local frontend at a deployed backend.
#
# NOTE: the value is the ORIGIN of the backend with no `/api` segment, since
# the backend routes are not prefixed. Do not add a trailing slash.
#
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-service.up.railway.app
